# Part of Cloudberry's greenplum_schedule (src/test/regress), as the port
# runs it on a coordinator and three segments: the tests of the schedule
# that bear on M2 -- dispatch, distribution, Motions, joins, aggregates,
# subqueries, partitions, DML -- in the schedule's order.
#
#   run   the test runs here, in both passes; cloudberry/ holds a difference
#         reviewed and kept, where one pass has one
#   skip  it needs what the port does not have yet: the rest of the line is
#         the first of Cloudberry's statements it refuses, as the port says
#
# The schedule's other tests -- append-optimized and column-oriented tables,
# external tables, resource queues and groups, fault injection, FTS, the
# interconnect's settings -- need M3 to M7, and are not listed.
